From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:47:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ggml-cpu: arm: faster PQ2_0 x Q8_K NEON kernel and 2x2 tile

Replace the TBL/SHL/AND/SUB unpacking of PQ2_0 codes with a de-interleaved
formulation: shift+mask a 16-byte load into four code vectors and pair them with
VLD4-de-interleaved Q8_K activations. The -1 code offset is removed with the
Q8_K bsums instead of a per-vector subtract, and four blocks are scaled per
float32x4 lane. Adds an nrc == 2 (2 rows x 2 columns) tile so prompt processing
decodes each weight vector once for two tokens; PQ2_0 advertises nrows = 2 on
AArch64 NEON. Per (row, col) the float sequence is identical in both paths, so
batched and single-token results are bit-identical. The Q8_0 fallback used for
rows that are not a multiple of 256 serves nrc == 2 one dot at a time.

Part of Bonsai-Oryon (https://github.com/SatoruGoj0/Bonsai-Oryon).
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch/arm/quants.c | 224 ++++++++++++++++++++++------
 ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c        |   4 +
 2 files changed, 183 insertions(+), 45 deletions(-)

